__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv*/
dist/
dist_check/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Downloaded from NCBI, not authored here. `scripts/fetch.py` rebuilds it, and
# the HTTP cache makes a rebuild cost NCBI nothing. Committing ~250 MB of
# sequence would also mean committing somebody else's database.
# Corpus data. Named files were listed one by one, which left any NEW corpus file
# committable - and a fetch at corpus scale writes gigabytes. The manifest
# (data/accessions.tsv) is what belongs in git; it rebuilds the rest exactly.
data/*
!data/accessions.tsv
# The 291,827-record manifest, gzipped: 13.4 MB of text, 1.54 MB compressed. Committed
# because results/drift_big.json is published from that corpus, and a results file whose
# corpus the repository cannot rebuild is not reproducible whatever its `reproduce` field
# says. Both scripts read a .gz manifest transparently.
!data/accessions_big.tsv.gz
!data/FINGERPRINT.tsv

# Scratch launcher for the background fetch, not part of the project.
run_fetch.bat

# Coverage artefacts. A 52 KB SQLite file holding absolute local paths; it was
# committed into four of these repositories the day coverage was first measured.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
